WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.322
Multiple CTEs can depend on earlier CTEs.

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:09.542
This creates a pipeline. The first stage summarizes admissions.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.627
The second stage joins those counts to patient attributes.

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:17.182
The final query creates a visit-pattern label.

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:22.307
Each stage has one focused job and one explainable grain.

00:00:22.307 --> 00:00:29.097
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:29.097 --> 00:00:37.242
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:37.242 --> 00:00:44.720
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
